      "text": "To determine the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\), we need to use the information given about the angles and the properties of a straight line.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - \\(RSP\\) is a straight line.\n   - \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n   - Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, the adjacent angle at \\(R\\), \\(\\angle PRQ\\), is directly opposite \\(\\angle QSP\\) and together they form a straight angle, which measures \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Determine \\(\\angle PRQ\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\angle PRQ = 180^\\circ - \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n3. **Analyze the triangle \\(PQR\\):**\n   - \\(\\angle PQR\\) and \\(\\angle PRQ\\) are the angles at vertex \\(Q\\).\n   - The sum of the angles in a triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\).\n   - Therefore, we can find \\(\\angle PQR\\) by subtracting \\(\\angle PRQ\\) from \\(180^\\circ\\):\n     \\[\n     \\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - \\angle PRQ = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{80}\\).",
