      "text": "To determine the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\), we start by analyzing the given information and the diagram. We know that \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, which means that \\(\\angle RSP = 180^\\circ\\). Additionally, we are given that \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n\nFirst, let's find the measure of \\(\\angle QSR\\). Since \\(\\angle RSP\\) is a straight angle, it can be broken down into two adjacent angles, \\(\\angle QSR\\) and \\(\\angle QSP\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle QSR + \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSubstituting the given value of \\(\\angle QSP\\):\n\\[\n\\angle QSR + 80^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\(\\angle QSR\\):\n\\[\n\\angle QSR = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\). Notice that \\(\\angle PQR\\) is part of \\(\\angle QSR\\). Specifically, \\(\\angle PQR\\) and \\(\\angle QSR\\) are supplementary angles, meaning their measures add up to \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle PQR + \\angle QSR = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSubstituting the known value of \\(\\angle QSR\\):\n\\[\n\\angle PQR + 100^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\(\\angle PQR\\):\n\\[\n\\angle PQR = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{80}\\).",
