      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) given that \\(RSP\\) is a straight line and \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n\nFirst, let's determine the measure of \\(\\angle SQR\\). Since \\(RSP\\) is a straight line, the sum of the angles on a straight line is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle SQR + \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSubstituting the given value of \\(\\angle QSP\\):\n\\[\n\\angle SQR + 80^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\nSolving for \\(\\angle SQR\\):\n\\[\n\\angle SQR = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\). Notice that \\(\\angle PQR\\) is the same as \\(\\angle SQR\\) because they are vertical angles (opposite angles formed by the intersection of two lines). Therefore:\n\\[\n\\angle PQR = \\angle SQR = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{100}\\).",
